# Performance and Operations

- Optimize Core Web Vitals by default:
  - keep components server-rendered when possible,
  - stream slow sections with Suspense,
  - minimize client JavaScript.
- Choose rendering strategy explicitly (dynamic, ISR, static, or PPR where available) based on data volatility and UX needs.
- Use `next/image` for content images; set explicit dimensions and prioritize only true LCP assets.
- Implement file-based loading/error boundaries (`loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`) for route segments with remote data dependencies.
- In Server Actions and handlers, return safe user-facing errors and structured logs for debugging.
- Validate required environment variables at runtime; fail fast instead of allowing silent misconfiguration.
- Prefer structured server-side logging and error reporting (for example Sentry/Axiom patterns already used in the codebase).
- For major UI/data changes, include a measurement plan (Lighthouse and/or bundle analysis).
